<section class="testimonial-area  py-0 mt-md-5" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(77, 79, 95, 1), rgba(77, 79, 95, 1)) !important;">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <div class="testimonial-wrapper-two">
            <div class="row " style="row-gap: 30px;">

                <div class="col-lg-6 pl-lg-3 d-flex align-items-center pr-lg-5 order-1-class">
                    <div class="testimonial-content-box bg_cover wow fadeInRight justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column" style="visibility: visible; animation-name: fadeInRight; background-image: none !important;">
                        <div class="section-title section-title-left pb-1" style="text-align: start !important;">
                            <h3 style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 26px;color: white !important;" class="mb-5">What is a Studmale and what does he need?</h3>
                            <p class="mt-1 mb-4" style="color: white !important; font-weight: bold;">A stud refers to a male cat that is retained for breeding purposes. He possesses desirable physical and behavioral traits that breeders wish to pass on to the next generation of their kittens. The term “stud” highlights the cat’s role in breeding, as he is used to providing litters. Typically, a stud is selected based on various attributes, including:</p>
                        </div>
                        <p style="color: white !important; font-weight: bold; display: flex;"> <strong style="font-size: medium; margin-right: 10px;">•</strong> Physical Attributes: A stud male should ideally represent the best physical qualities of his breed. This includes the size of the cat and his offspring, coat quality and looks, and physical characteristics.</p>
                        <p style="color: white !important; font-weight: bold; display: flex;" class="mt-2"> <strong style="font-size: medium; margin-right: 10px;">•</strong> Health: It’s essential that a Stud male is free from genetic disorders or diseases that can be passed on to his offspring. Regular health checks like FIV/FeLV tests and certain health clearances might be mandatory in many formal breeding settings. Some breeds ask specific checks, like HCM and PKD for example. You can ask your association what kind of tests are required for your breed.</p>

                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center order-2-class">
                    <img src="/webassets/images/elements/steo-10.jpg" alt="img" style="border: 2px solid white; ">
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</section>
<section id="features" class="features section py-5 ">
    <div class="container py-md-4">
        <div class="row   align-items-stretch   " style="row-gap: 30px;  ">
            <div class="col-lg-6 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center  " data-aos="zoom-out">
                <img src="/webassets/images/elements/step-12.jpeg" class="img-height" alt="img">
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5 d-flex justify-content-center flex-column  " data-aos="fade-up">
                <h3 style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 26px;color: black !important;" class="mb-3">More Details</h3>

                <p style="color: black !important; font-weight: bold; display: flex;" class="mt-2"> <strong style="font-size: medium; margin-right: 10px;">•</strong>  <span><b>Temperament: </b>A good Stud male should also possess a temperament that is typical and desirable for the breed. This ensures that not just physical but also behavioral traits are passed on to the next generation. It's important to ask and describe what type of cat fits in your breeding program.</span></p>
                <p style="color: black !important; font-weight: bold; display: flex;" class="mt-2">
                    <strong style="font-size: medium; margin-right: 10px;">•</strong> <span><b>Breeding Success:</b> Past success in previous litters that are healthy, of good size, and adhere closely to breed standards can also be a factor in a cat's desirability as a stud.</span>
                </p>
                <p style="color: black !important; font-weight: bold; display: flex;" class="mt-2"> <strong style="font-size: medium; margin-right: 10px;">•</strong> <span>As you can see, a Stud male should be in the best condition if you want to add him to your breeding program. ​It's important that you ask the owner if they can show you what kind of checks they have done with their Stud.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div><!-- Features Item -->
    </div>

</section>